DISTRIBUTED DEPENDENCIES

Runtime, SDK, compiler, website and operating-system dependencies have their own
licenses. For a particular bundle, consult its licenses/ directory, source-bound
sbom.spdx.json and build inventory. Native runtime bundles retain LICENSE and
NOTICE at their root; developer bundles retain licenses/LSF.txt and
licenses/LSF-NOTICE.txt. These files accompany, rather than replace, upstream
license and notice texts collected by the respective builders.

Exact dependency inputs are recorded in the owning Cargo/npm/language locks and
toolchain manifests. packaging/linux/license-sources.json records reviewed
shared-monorepo license donors for exact native dependency versions. Compiler
and system-image builders retain their separate upstream notices and package
inventories; static font preparation retains the selected font's license.
This file is an attribution index, not an exhaustive dependency inventory.
